    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21478" root="سيو" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِيَةٌ</span></b>  The <i>curved part of each of the two extremities</i> of a bow: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِيَاتٌ</span>: (S, K:) the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span> in
the sing. is a substitute for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">و</span>: AO says that
Ru-beh used to pronounce it [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِئَةٌ</span>,] with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span>; and
the rest of the Arabs, [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِيَةٌ</span>,] without <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span>. (S, TA.)
[See also art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سأو</span>.]

